---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ApiDemo from '../components/marketing/ApiDemo.astro';
import Closing from '../components/Closing.astro';
import { codingAgentGuidePath } from '../data/coding-agent';
import '../styles/marketing.css';
const features=[
 {number:'01',icon:'route',title:'Send a URL.',text:'Auto mode picks the route and moves to a browser when it must. Set route or render only when you need to.',link:'How auto mode works',href:'/docs/fetch#auto-mode'},
 {number:'02',icon:'file',title:'Read the result.',text:'Get the body, markdown or a screenshot, every attempt, and what it cost. A failure says what to do next.',link:'Read the fetch reference',href:'/docs/fetch'},
 {number:'03',icon:'lock',title:'Retry safely.',text:'Send an idempotency_key. Resending after a lost response returns the first result and is never charged twice.',link:'Errors and next steps',href:'/docs/errors'},
];
---
<Layout title="Built for developers — FetchX" description="Connect FetchX to your application with one API call. Explore cURL, JavaScript and Python examples.">
 <div class="mkt"><div class="mkt-container"><header class="mkt-page-intro mkt-developer-intro"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow"><Icon name="code" size={16}/> THE API IS THE INTERFACE</span><h1>Your stack.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">The whole web ahead.</span></h1><p>Bring web access into the tools you already use. One call, every attempt reported, and safe retries.</p><div class="mkt-actions">
  <a class="mkt-button mkt-button-primary" href="/docs">Open the quickstart <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a>
  <a class="mkt-button mkt-button-secondary" href={codingAgentGuidePath}>Quickstart for coding agents <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a>
  <a class="mkt-button mkt-button-secondary" href="/docs/reference">Read the API reference <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a>
 </div></div><div class="mkt-developer-aside"><span class="mkt-micro">BRING YOUR OWN STACK</span><div><span>cURL</span><span>JavaScript</span><span>Python</span><span>Any HTTP client</span></div><p>Small clients for JavaScript and Python,<br/>or any HTTP client.</p><code>POST /v1/fetch</code></div></header>
 <section class="mkt-developer-example"><div class="mkt-section-heading"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">01 / MAKE THE CONNECTION</span><h2>One request.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">Start here.</span></h2></div><p>Create an API key in the console, set FETCHX_URL and FETCHX_TOKEN, and make the call.</p></div><ApiDemo id="developer-example"/></section>
 <section class="mkt-section"><div class="mkt-developer-features">{features.map(feature=><article><div class="mkt-problem-top"><Icon name={feature.icon} size={24}/><span>{feature.number}</span></div><h3>{feature.title}</h3><p>{feature.text}</p><a class="mkt-text-link" href={feature.href}>{feature.link}<Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></a></article>)}</div></section>
 <section class="mkt-developer-paths"><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">02 / ONE ENDPOINT</span><h2>HTTP when it works.<br/><span class="mkt-muted">A browser when it must.</span></h2><p>The same call covers plain pages, JavaScript apps and pages behind challenges.</p></div><div class="mkt-path-cards"><a href="/docs/fetch"><span class="mkt-tag">AUTO MODE</span><code>/v1/fetch</code><h3>The cheapest route that works.</h3><p>HTTP first, then residential IPs and a browser, with what worked remembered per site.</p><span class="mkt-text-link">Fetch API reference <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></span></a><a href="/docs/coding-agents"><span class="mkt-tag">AGENTS</span><code>Connect</code><h3>Give an agent a key safely.</h3><p>The user approves in the browser; the agent gets FETCHX_URL and FETCHX_TOKEN.</p><span class="mkt-text-link">Coding agent guide <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></span></a></div></section>
 <section class="mkt-open-source"><div class="mkt-open-source-icon"><Icon name="code" size={38}/></div><div><span class="mkt-eyebrow">INTEGRATION GUIDES</span><h2>Plan your integration.</h2><p>Explore guides on rendering, proxy routing and reliable web requests.</p></div><a class="mkt-button mkt-button-secondary" href="/resources">Explore the guides <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a></section>
 </div><Closing/></div><script>import '../scripts/marketing.ts';</script>
</Layout>
